    "type": "md",
    "content": "# Python Sorting and Searching Algorithms - Complete Guide\n\n## \ud83d\udccb Overview\n\nSorting and searching are fundamental operations in computer science. This guide covers the implementation, complexity, and use cases for common algorithms in Python. All explanations are available in **Hinglish** for better understanding.\n\n## \ud83d\udd22 Sorting Algorithms (\u0938\u0949\u0930\u094d\u091f\u093f\u0902\u0917 \u090f\u0932\u094d\u0917\u094b\u0930\u093f\u0926\u092e)\n\n| Algorithm          | Description                                                  | Link                                               |\n| :----------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Bubble Sort**    | Simple swapping of adjacent elements.                        | [Read Concept (Hinglish)](BubbleSort.md)    |\n| **Selection Sort** | Selecting the smallest element and moving it to sorted part. | [Read Concept (Hinglish)](SelectionSort.md) |\n| **Insertion Sort** | Inserting element at correct position (like playing cards).  | [Read Concept (Hinglish)](InsertionSort.md) |\n| **Merge Sort**     | Divide and Conquer strategy. Stable sort.                    | [Read Concept (Hinglish)](MergeSort.md)     |\n| **Quick Sort**     | Divide and Conquer using pivots. Very fast.                  | [Read Concept (Hinglish)](QuickSort.md)     |\n| **Counting Sort**  | Integer sorting based on keys range.                         | [Read Concept (Hinglish)](CountingSort.md)  |\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 Theoretical Concepts\n\n- \ud83d\udc49 **[Understand Stable vs Unstable Sorting (Hinglish Guide)](Stable_vs_Unstable.md)**\n- \ud83d\udc49 **[Understand Adaptive vs Non-Adaptive Sorting (Hinglish Guide)](Adaptive_vs_NonAdaptive.md)**\n\n## \ud83d\udd0d Searching Algorithms (\u0938\u0930\u094d\u091a\u093f\u0902\u0917 \u090f\u0932\u094d\u0917\u094b\u0930\u093f\u0926\u092e)\n\n| Algorithm         | Description                                            | Link                                              |\n| :---------------- | :----------------------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Linear Search** | Sequential check. Works on unsorted lists.             | [Read Concept (Hinglish)](LinearSearch.md) |\n| **Binary Search** | Divide and conquer search. Works ONLY on sorted lists. | [Read Concept (Hinglish)](BinarySearch.md) |\n\n## \u2696\ufe0f Complexity Comparison\n\n| Algorithm          | Best Time  | Average Time | Worst Time | Space    | Stable? | Adaptive? |\n| :----------------- | :--------- | :----------- | :--------- | :------- | :------ | :-------- |\n| **Bubble Sort**    | O(n)       | O(n\u00b2)        | O(n\u00b2)      | O(1)     | Yes     | Yes       |\n| **Selection Sort** | O(n\u00b2)      | O(n\u00b2)        | O(n\u00b2)      | O(1)     | No      | No        |\n| **Insertion Sort** | O(n)       | O(n\u00b2)        | O(n\u00b2)      | O(1)     | Yes     | Yes       |\n| **Merge Sort**     | O(n log n) | O(n log n)   | O(n log n) | O(n)     | Yes     | No        |\n| **Quick Sort**     | O(n log n) | O(n log n)   | O(n\u00b2)      | O(log n) | No      | No        |\n| **Linear Search**  | O(1)       | O(n)         | O(n)       | O(1)     | N/A     | N/A       |\n| **Binary Search**  | O(1)       | O(log n)     | O(log n)   | O(1)     | N/A     | N/A       |\n"
