    "content": "\"\"\"You are given a string and your task is to swap cases. In other words, convert all lowercase letters to uppercase letters and vice versa.\n\nFor Example:\n\nWww.HackerRank.com \u2192 wWW.hACKERrANK.COM\nPythonist 2 \u2192 pYTHONIST 2  \nFunction Description\n\nComplete the swap_case function in the editor below.\n\nswap_case has the following parameters:\n\nstring s: the string to modify\nReturns\n\nstring: the modified string\nInput Format\n\nA single line containing a string .\n\nConstraints\n\n\nSample Input 0\n\nHackerRank.com presents \"Pythonist 2\".\nSample Output 0\n\nhACKERrANK.COM PRESENTS \"pYTHONIST 2\".\"\"\"\n\n#Solution 1:\n# def swap_case(s):\n#     return s.swapcase()\n\n# if __name__ == '__main__':\n#     s = input()\n#     result = swap_case(s)\n#     print(result)\n\n#Solution 2:\ndef swap_case(s):\n    result = \"\"\n    \n    for char in s:\n        if char.islower():\n            result += char.upper()\n        elif char.isupper():\n            result += char.lower()\n        else:\n            result += char   # digits, spaces, symbols remain unchanged\n            \n    return result\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    s = input()\n    result = swap_case(s)\n    print(result)"
